.SH NAME
le-keep-awake - Stop your Mac sleeping (caffeinate); no arg = until Ctrl-C


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBle keep-awake [duration] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Run caffeinate -d -i so the Mac won't sleep. Give a duration like 15m,
1h, or 90s; with no argument it stays awake until you press Ctrl-C.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for keep-awake


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBle(1)\fP


